        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "99ef0bb4-956e-567b-af73-a30989a292f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dee Dee Ramone, Ben Weasel\n- Bands: Ramones, Screeching Weasel\n- Songs: “Rockaway Beach”\n- Media: “Weasel Radio”\n- Topics: punk rock, surf rock\n\nFacts:\n- Douglas Glenn Colvin was born on September 18, 1951, and was professionally known as Dee Dee Ramone.\n- Dee Dee Ramone was a German-American musician, singer, and songwriter.\n- Dee Dee Ramone was a founding member, songwriter, bassist, and occasional lead vocalist for the punk rock band the Ramones.\n- Ben Weasel was born Benjamin Foster.\n- Ben Weasel is a punk rock musician best known as the lead singer and guitarist of the band Screeching Weasel.\n- Ben Weasel co-hosts “Weasel Radio,” a weekly radio show that formerly aired on ESPN 1070 and was later relaunched as a podcast.\n- Dee Dee Ramone wrote the song “Rockaway Beach” in the style of the Beach Boys and early surf rock bands.\n- Dee Dee Ramone died on June 5, 2002.",
